      "body": "Fixes #7650.\n\nThe weighted SwiGLU kernel derives input addresses from a 32-bit `xoffset`. When an input row starts at element `2^31`, the address wraps and CUDA reports an illegal memory access. Cast `xoffset` to `int64` before calculating the address.\n\nThe new test reproduces the fault on `main` and passes on this branch. I also extended the existing replay test to cover a second block size, as required by the repository's determinism check.\n\nI ran the three weighted SwiGLU tests, the replay test, Black, and the kernel coverage check locally. The large test skips when less than 6.5 GiB of GPU memory is free. I did not run the full suite.\n",
